**Medium Severity**

<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->
The PR description explicitly states that if transcript redaction fails in `CondenseSession`, the transcript is dropped while checkpoint metadata (files touched, attributions, etc.) is still written. However, the implementation returns a hard error via `return nil, fmt.Errorf(...)`, which aborts the entire condensation — no checkpoint metadata is persisted at all. To match the documented safety design, a redaction failure here would need to log a warning, set `redactedTranscript` to its zero value, and continue with the rest of the function.
<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->

<!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: 6446cca4-86ad-4afe-a47e-9c3ea3519105 -->

